fixed: ["Answer rewritten for a like-for-like comparison. It leads with the most nights from one box with no add-on batteries: Anker SOLIX S5000, about 10.7 nights at 40 W, idling at about 10 W (existing table figures from pv magazine USA and Anker). A second sentence says expandable systems go further only by adding batteries and gives each battery count: S5000 + 1 expansion battery about 21, DELTA Pro Ultra X + 2 batteries 17.2, Apex 300 + 2 B300K 14.7. All three figures are already worked out in the after-section. The answer is 294 characters of text and uses the question's words.", "must updated to exact substrings of the new answer: 'The Anker SOLIX S5000 runs a CPAP for the most nights on one charge from one box' (the pick) and 'about 10.7 at 40 W, idling at about 10 W' (its deciding figure).", "Rows reordered with the S5000 first; the other rows keep their order. Added a column ['batteries', 'Batteries in this figure'], filled for every row: one box (S5000, Elite 300, Explorer 5000 Plus, F3800 Plus), inverter + 2 batteries (DELTA Pro Ultra X), Apex 300 + 2 B300K packs, inverter + 1 battery (DELTA Pro Ultra).", "Same like-for-like fix applied in the after-section, so it doesn't contradict the new answer. Added a paragraph saying single boxes are the fair comparison and the expandable figures include named add-on batteries. Moved the S5000 bullet first and labelled the battery counts in the bullets. The decision-table row 'most measured nights, whatever the price' now reads 'wi
